import{_ as a,o as r,c as t,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.Bx6eOp9J.js";const h=JSON.parse('{"title":"2026-11-02 Agent Research and Competitor Intelligence","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"2026-11-02 Agent Research and Competitor Intelligence"},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/runtime/daily-intelligence/2026-11-02.md","filePath":"en/runtime/daily-intelligence/2026-11-02.md","lastUpdated":1793588050000}'),i={name:"en/runtime/daily-intelligence/2026-11-02.md"};function s(o,e,l,d,c,p){return r(),t("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="_2026-11-02-agent-research-and-competitor-intelligence" tabindex="-1">2026-11-02 Agent Research and Competitor Intelligence <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2026-11-02-agent-research-and-competitor-intelligence" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2026-11-02 Agent Research and Competitor Intelligence&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Recovery identity, revocation and migration lead this run: Paperclip advances suspended-session recovery to a same-source live pass while hosted/production qualification remains pending; Langfuse checks key-owner revocation. All CodeFlowMu/FCoP implications are pending validation.</p><h2 id="_1-paperclip-restores-suspended-conversations-across-controllers" tabindex="-1">1. Paperclip restores suspended conversations across controllers <a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-paperclip-restores-suspended-conversations-across-controllers" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;1. Paperclip restores suspended conversations across controllers&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>#18554 MERGED; scoped live test passed; hosted/canary pending</strong></p><p>Restores verified Runner suspension receipts and retains old-authority launch files instead of treating a safely suspended Runner as live. The same-source Codex/Daytona test passes with 518 reads, 53 verified saves and four turns retaining provider conversation/native receipts. Hosted browser reconnect, ten-deploy Railway qualification and production canary remain pending; initial CI and cleanup failures are retained.</p><p>High learning value/risk; selectively raise main-radar recovery maturity. Pending FCoP lead: jointly validate suspension receipts, physical sandbox and session identity. Discuss interrupted receipt reads and old-authority file retirement.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/18554" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">PR #18554</a></p><h2 id="_2-langfuse-checks-the-owner-of-user-bound-gateway-keys" tabindex="-1">2. Langfuse checks the owner of user-bound gateway keys <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-langfuse-checks-the-owner-of-user-bound-gateway-keys" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2. Langfuse checks the owner of user-bound gateway keys&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>#19542 MERGED; release not verified</strong></p><p>Previously only key roles were checked, so out-of-band owner demotion/removal could leave keys usable. Resolve cache misses now check the owner&#39;s organization gateway:invoke right and reject with 403; service-account keys are unchanged. Out-of-band changes have the default 60-second cache TTL boundary; in-app demotions already delete keys and evict cache immediately.</p><p>Pending lead: valid credentials do not prove current owner authority; record revocation latency separately. Discuss invalidation, restored roles and service-account ownership.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/langfuse/langfuse/pull/19542" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">PR #19542</a></p><h2 id="_3-ag2-reconciles-a2a-streaming-and-polling-by-artifact-identity" tabindex="-1">3. AG2 reconciles A2A streaming and polling by artifact identity <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-ag2-reconciles-a2a-streaming-and-polling-by-artifact-identity" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3. AG2 reconciles A2A streaming and polling by artifact identity&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>#3494 MERGED; release not verified</strong></p><p>Each artifact keeps full content and a turn baseline; streaming updates and polling snapshots share one ledger to avoid first-poll truncation, duplicated tool calls and prior-turn text leakage. Cancellation is not an ordinary answer and actual requests stay bound to the validated interface. Server changes address terminal cancellation races and artifact completion semantics.</p><p>Pending FCoP lead: reconnect/polling need artifact and turn identity, not guessed string concatenation. Discuss ID reuse across turns, full retransmission and mixed parts.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/ag2ai/ag2/pull/3494" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">PR #3494</a></p><h2 id="_4-openhands-resumes-repeated-pauses-and-decouples-saved-history-from-unavailable-runtimes" tabindex="-1">4. OpenHands resumes repeated pauses and decouples saved history from unavailable runtimes <a class="header-anchor" href="#_4-openhands-resumes-repeated-pauses-and-decouples-saved-history-from-unavailable-runtimes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;4. OpenHands resumes repeated pauses and decouples saved history from unavailable runtimes&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>#19186/#19194 MERGED; release not verified</strong></p><p>New messages/retries can resume a sandbox paused again by capacity policy; pending resumes coalesce, idle tabs do not repeatedly wake it and obsolete navigation/organization attempts are ignored. Saved-history loading skips count requests to PAUSED/MISSING/ERROR runtimes. Small ordinary-conversation samples do not establish normal-load speedup; injected-delay results are not everyday performance claims.</p><p>Pending lead: separate user-triggered recovery from observation, and saved history from runtime liveness. Discuss timeout isolation between retries and history/replay coverage.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/OpenHands/pull/19186" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">PR #19186</a> · <a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/OpenHands/pull/19194" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">PR #19194</a></p><h2 id="_5-paradev-migrates-app-home-and-project-configuration-with-legacy-compatibility" tabindex="-1">5. Paradev migrates app home and project configuration with legacy compatibility <a class="header-anchor" href="#_5-paradev-migrates-app-home-and-project-configuration-with-legacy-compatibility" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;5. Paradev migrates app home and project configuration with legacy compatibility&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>#9158/#9248 MERGED; release not verified</strong></p><p>App home moves from ~/.superset to ~/.paradev after validating old host-service PID command lines; pty daemon, legacy symlink, Claude session mapping and worktree/database repair preserve continuity. Failures retain the old home and retry later. Project configuration selection prioritizes actual main config files over directory existence or stray ports files. SUPERSET_HOME_DIR remains supported.</p><p>High learning value, medium-high risk; raise main-radar migration/compatibility attention. Pending lead: rebranding crosses paths, sessions and long-lived processes. Discuss concurrent migration, clashes, old-client attachments and rollback.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/ParadevAI/Paradev/pull/9158" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">PR #9158</a> · <a href="https://github.com/ParadevAI/Paradev/pull/9248" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">PR #9248</a></p><h2 id="_6-orkas-summarizes-private-ipc-errors-in-logs-while-preserving-caller-details" tabindex="-1">6. Orkas summarizes private IPC errors in logs while preserving caller details <a class="header-anchor" href="#_6-orkas-summarizes-private-ipc-errors-in-logs-while-preserving-caller-details" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;6. Orkas summarizes private IPC errors in logs while preserving caller details&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>#154 MERGED; release not verified</strong></p><p>IPC logging summarizes failure text for returned errors, exceptions, imports and failed streams while preserving original replies to callers. Upstream privacy regressions and real Electron startup/automation relaunch journeys pass; these are not local experiments or a comprehensive leakage audit.</p><p>Medium-high learning value, medium risk; retain main-radar privacy/diagnostics attention. Pending lead: caller diagnostics and collected logs need different boundaries. Discuss nested errors, retry deduplication and stream cleanup.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/Orkas-AI/Orkas/pull/154" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">PR #154</a></p><h2 id="signals-classification-and-coverage" tabindex="-1">Signals, classification and coverage <a class="header-anchor" href="#signals-classification-and-coverage" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Signals, classification and coverage&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Recovery preserves session/artifact/path identity. Credential validity is not owner authority. Injected experiments, scoped passes and production qualification remain separate. Local experiments, articles, development reviews and external comments are all zero.</p><p>Actual start: 2026-11-02 10:46:49 Asia/Shanghai; deduplicated from the November 1 22:26:48 baseline. Latest Registry was first read through GitHub tools: 47 people. Relationships remain many-to-many; Yue Zhao is consistently 赵越, with no new code confirmed. Six governance subjects retain their boundaries; bulbasaur is not the official AGENTSAFE artifact. Commit checks for 88 targets are saved; Orca&#39;s first 100 are unfinished and TSA returns 404. Issues are bounded at ten and releases at three per target; full pages remain partial and do not advance complete watermarks. Large-batch connector calls repeatedly terminated, then were rerun in four-way batches and saved. Coverage is weaker than earlier full pagination, not exhaustive. Maintainer participation rests on original PR author/merger facts. Discussions, roadmaps, architecture and licenses are not exhaustive; merges are not called releases.</p><p>Public person/X queries and direct Cursor/Audit Commons checks are separate. No reliably timed personal new post is confirmed; this is not exhaustive social coverage. Visible old materials are not new; two GitHub links are not two source types.</p><p>Only the two dated reports and indexes are written. Existing site/layout/snapshots/entry points remain; main readback, matching gh-pages/Pages and bilingual click evidence are saved locally, without preclaiming deployment. No Research Runtime lifecycle, scheduler or candidate facts are changed.</p>',37)])])}const g=a(i,[["render",s]]);export{h as __pageData,g as default};
